---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 6</p>
  <h1>Adverbs of <em>frequency</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Show how often something happens: <span class="ex">I usually cook</span>, <span class="ex">She is always early</span>, and <span class="ex">We never drive</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">always → never</span>
    <span class="tag">word order</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read three sentences about a routine.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Find where the adverb sits.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Place, type, and build the pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe your real week.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">One small word, <span class="ex">always</span>, <span class="ex">usually</span>, <span class="ex">sometimes</span>, or <span class="ex">never</span>, tells the listener how often something happens. The only trick is where to put it.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="checks">checks</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="check">check</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can">can</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Daniel <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="checks" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> his email every morning. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(present simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> speak Spanish and English. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(can)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> busy on Mondays. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the verb to be)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Three sentences about a morning</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"I always check my email before breakfast. My boss is usually in the office at eight. I never take the bus."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which three words tell you how often?</li>
      <li>Where does each frequency word sit? Look carefully: it comes before <span class="ex">check</span> and before <span class="ex">take</span>, but after <span class="ex">is</span>.</li>
      <li>Which sentence uses a form of <span class="ex">be</span>? What is different about it?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: match the meaning</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the situation first. Then choose the adverb that describes it.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always">always</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="usually">usually</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sometimes">sometimes</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="never">never</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The 8:15 train leaves on time every single day. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> leaves on time.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I drink coffee most mornings, but not every morning. I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="usually" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> drink coffee.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>He eats out two or three times a month. He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sometimes" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> eats out.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>She does not watch television at all. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="never" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> watches television.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We are on time for every meeting, with no exceptions. We are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on time.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I have not worked on a Sunday once this year. I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="never" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> work on Sundays.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: a ladder from always to never</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Frequency adverbs help the listener build a picture from many occasions. Imagine looking at every Monday for a year: if the same event appears on every Monday, it <span class="ex">always</span> happens, and if it appears on none, it <span class="ex">never</span> happens. The other words describe the middle of the scale.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adverb</th><th>how often</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>always</b></td><td>100%, every time</td><td>I always lock the office door.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>usually</b></td><td>almost every time</td><td>I usually start work at nine.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>often</b></td><td>many times</td><td>She often works from home.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>sometimes</b></td><td>some of the time</td><td>We sometimes eat lunch outside.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>rarely</b></td><td>almost never</td><td>He rarely takes a taxi.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>never</b></td><td>0%, at no time</td><td>They never open on Sundays.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">The percentages are memory aids, not measurements. <span class="ex">Usually</span> is not a mathematical 80%, and two speakers may choose different words for the same real pattern.</p>

  <h2>Get to the root: one rule, two positions</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The heart of this lesson is position. A frequency adverb sits <strong>before a normal verb</strong> but <strong>after the verb be</strong>. Say <span class="ex">I always start at nine</span> and <span class="ex">She is always on time</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>main verb</th><th>position</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>a normal verb</b> (check, take, work)</td><td>adverb before the verb</td><td>I always start at nine.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>the verb be</b> (am, is, are)</td><td>adverb after be</td><td>She is always on time.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Sometimes</span> is the flexible one: it can also move to the front. <span class="ex">Sometimes I work late</span> means the same as <span class="ex">I sometimes work late</span>.</p>

  <h3>Why the order changes with <em>be</em></h3>
  <p>With most verbs, the adverb stands in front of the action: <span class="ex">I usually cook</span>. With <span class="ex">be</span>, the verb is short and structurally central, so the adverb follows it: <span class="ex">I am usually tired</span>. In longer verb phrases, it normally follows the first helper verb: <span class="ex">She can always help</span>.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Already negative</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Never</span> and <span class="ex">rarely</span> carry a negative meaning by themselves: <span class="ex">I never drink coffee</span> already means “not on any occasion.” English uses one negative per idea, so say <span class="ex">I never drink coffee</span>, not <span class="ex">I don’t never drink coffee</span>. If the sentence already has <span class="ex">don’t</span>, it does not need <span class="ex">never</span> too.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the chunk in the right position</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Find the verb first. Is it <b>be</b> or a normal verb? Then choose the chunk that puts the adverb in the natural place.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is never">is never</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="never is">never is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="usually work">usually work</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="work usually">work usually</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always checks">always checks</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="checks always">checks always</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is often">is often</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="often is">often is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sometimes takes">sometimes takes</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="takes sometimes">takes sometimes</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Rosa <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is never" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late. You can set your watch by her.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="usually work" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home on Fridays.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>My manager <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always checks" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the numbers before a meeting.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is often" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> tired after the night shift, so he sleeps until noon.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Elena <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sometimes takes" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the early train when she has a morning meeting.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>My coworkers <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="usually work" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late on Thursdays because of the weekly report.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The break room <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is often" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> noisy at lunchtime, so I eat at my desk.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Sam <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sometimes takes" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bus when it rains.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Frequency adverbs and frequency phrases</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>These two tools answer the same broad question, but they give different kinds of information.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>tool</th><th>position</th><th>information</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>adverb</b></td><td>inside the verb phrase</td><td><span class="ex">I often call her.</span> A general pattern.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>frequency phrase</b></td><td>usually at the end</td><td><span class="ex">I call her twice a week.</span> A measurable rate.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>every + time</b></td><td>usually at the end</td><td><span class="ex">I call her every Sunday.</span> A repeated schedule.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>You can combine them when the meaning is sensible: <span class="ex">I usually exercise three times a week.</span> The adverb describes how normal the pattern is; the phrase measures the pattern.</p>

  <h3>Ask with <em>How often…?</em></h3>
  <p>Use <span class="ex">How often + do/does + subject + base verb?</span>: <span class="ex">How often do you cook?</span> With <span class="ex">be</span>, move <span class="ex">be</span> directly: <span class="ex">How often are you late?</span> Answers can be general (<span class="ex">Rarely</span>) or exact (<span class="ex">About once a month</span>).</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>A meaning trap</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Hardly ever</span> means the same as <span class="ex">rarely</span>: almost never. Do not confuse it with <span class="ex">hard</span>, which describes effort. <span class="ex">He works hard</span> is about effort; <span class="ex">He hardly ever works late</span> is about frequency.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the adverb</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the cue, then type one adverb from the ladder: <b>always</b>, <b>usually</b>, <b>often</b>, <b>sometimes</b>, <b>rarely</b>, or <b>never</b>.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>100%, every time: I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="always" aria-label="answer 1" /> lock the door when I leave.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>0%, at no time: I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="never" aria-label="answer 2" /> eat meat. I’m vegetarian.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Almost every time: I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="usually" aria-label="answer 3" /> have coffee with breakfast.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Some of the time: I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="sometimes" aria-label="answer 4" /> walk to work.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Many times: she <input class="answer-input" data-answer="often" aria-label="answer 5" /> travels for work.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Almost never: he <input class="answer-input" data-answer="rarely" aria-label="answer 6" /> takes a taxi.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A coworker’s routine</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"My coworker Elena usually opens the office. She always makes the first pot of coffee, and she is never late, even in bad weather. On Fridays she sometimes leaves early to pick up her son from school. She rarely takes the elevator because she likes the stairs."</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You followed the frequency words in a real description.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Elena">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Who usually opens the office?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Elena">Elena</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="her son">her son</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the writer">the writer</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="never">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. How often is Elena late?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="never">never</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sometimes">sometimes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="often">often</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the elevator">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What does she rarely take?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the elevator">the elevator</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the stairs">the stairs</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the early train">the early train</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she is always on time">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the sentence with be</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. Remember: the adverb comes after is.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="time">time</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="always">always</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i usually walk to work">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the sentence with a normal verb</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. The adverb comes before a normal verb.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="walk">walk</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="usually">usually</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="work">work</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="always" data-fix="I always go to the gym after work." data-why="Put the frequency adverb before a normal verb like go.">
    <h3>Drill 6: repair the normal-verb sentence</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is in the wrong place.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="go">go</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="always">always</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="gym">to the gym</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="work">after work.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="always" data-fix="She is always tired on Monday mornings." data-why="With be, the frequency adverb comes after am, is, or are.">
    <h3>Drill 7: repair the be sentence</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is in the wrong place.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="always">always</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="tired">tired</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="mondays">on Monday mornings.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Add the adverb in the right place, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I check my email. Add always.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I always check my email.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> She is on time. Add never.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She is never on time.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> We take the bus. Add usually.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We usually take the bus.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> He is busy on Fridays. Add often.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He is often busy on Fridays.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> I take a taxi. Add rarely.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I rarely take a taxi.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> My boss is in the office at eight. Add usually.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>My boss is usually in the office at eight.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your mornings:</b> Say five true sentences about your morning with <span class="ex">always</span> and <span class="ex">usually</span>. <span class="ex">I always make coffee first. I usually leave at eight.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your never list:</b> Say three things you never do on a workday. <span class="ex">I never skip breakfast. I never answer email after ten.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask five <span class="ex">How often…?</span> questions and listen for the adverb in the answer. <span class="ex">How often do you cook? How often are you late?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Someone you know:</b> Describe a coworker or family member with three frequency adverbs. <span class="ex">My brother is always calm. He rarely complains.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Weekday and weekend:</b> Compare a normal weekday with a Saturday. <span class="ex">On weekdays I always get up at seven. On Saturdays I usually sleep late.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “With a normal verb, the frequency adverb comes ______ the verb. With am, is, and are, it comes ______ the verb. The flexible word that can also start a sentence is ______. The word that means 0% is ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence with <span class="ex">always</span>, one with <span class="ex">never</span>, and one with <span class="ex">is usually</span> about your real week.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can say how often, and put the adverb in the right place.">
    <h3>Final quiz: position and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I usually walk to work">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Choose the natural order.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I usually walk to work">I usually walk to work</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I walk usually to work">I walk usually to work</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I usually am walk to work">I usually am walk to work</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is never">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. She ___ late.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is never">is never</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="never is">never is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="never be">never be</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="never">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Which word means 0% of the time?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="never">never</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rarely">rarely</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sometimes">sometimes</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="always">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Which word means 100% of the time?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="always">always</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="usually">usually</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="often">often</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I never drink coffee.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I never drink coffee.">I never drink coffee.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I don’t never drink coffee.">I don’t never drink coffee.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I drink never coffee.">I drink never coffee.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="usually works">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. He ___ from home on Fridays.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="usually works">usually works</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="works usually">works usually</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is usually works">is usually works</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Sometimes">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Which adverb can move to the front, as in “___ I work late”?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Sometimes">Sometimes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Never">Never</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Always">Always</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="rarely">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. Which word means almost never?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rarely">rarely</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="often">often</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="usually">usually</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
